  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Node.js Setup**\n\nI\'ve successfully configured the foundational Node.js setup using `package.json`, incorporating essential packages like `express`, `dotenv`, `tsx`, and `esbuild`. Following the full-stack guide, I\'ve defined both development and build scripts. The `dev` script utilizes `tsx` for server execution, while the `build` script combines `vite` and `esbuild` for optimal bundling and output.\n\n\n**Structuring the Backend Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the backend and frontend components with a modular structure. I\'ve defined the necessary URLs and features, like `/control/line-a/pickup`, and `/control/line-b/dropoff`. The backend responsibilities include parsing `config.json` for the AMR system details, setting up URL matching, defining parameters such as `mockMode`, and constructing routes for processing commands.\n\n\n**Defining Line and Order States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the structure for line configurations and shared in-memory state. I\'ve defined data structures for \"line-a\" and \"line-b,\" including task paths and stations. Also included are state variables like `status`, `currentOrderId`, and `lockedAt`. Additionally, I\'m working on an `orderId` generator that utilizes a sequential lock to ensure unique identifiers, including timestamp and milliseconds.\n\n\n**Implementing Order Processing Logic**\n\nI\'ve finalized the order ID generation, now strictly adhering to the \"cong_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_mmm\" format, and incorporated line locking logic. It prevents concurrent commands by rejecting requests when a line is busy. I\'ve designed the atomic check-and-lock to handle race conditions. I\'m also implementing the AMR system client, including mock mode and detailed error handling, with strict payload structures for both order and trigger requests.\n\n**Designing API Endpoints**\n\nI am now implementing all required API endpoints including GET, POST, and helper routes. The GET endpoints include /api/config and /api/state, allowing access to the configuration and system status, respectively. The POST endpoints enable command execution via /api/order, trigger action with /api/trigger, system reset using /api/line/reset and mock mode toggle via /api/mock/toggle. I have also added an /api/logs route for communication history.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 806541571
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
