  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started defining the necessary API endpoints based on Decision 5 and the given guidelines. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the `/api/config` endpoint, including validation of the `line` and `station` parameters against `config.lines`. I\'m starting to structure the response as well, ensuring it meets the specified JSON format.\n\n\n**Refining API Response Structure**\n\nI\'ve refined the `GET /api/config` response, ensuring it includes `lineKey`, `stationKey`, and other descriptive fields like `lineName` and `stationName`. The structure now provides comprehensive data including the `taskPath` and `triggerStation`. I\'m also implementing the endpoint for retrieving all lines and stations when no parameters are provided to `GET /api/config`. The `GET /api/state` and `POST /api/order` endpoints are the focus of my attention next.\n\n\n**Implementing Order Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `POST /api/order` functionality. I\'m focusing on assembling the full AMR order payload using `config.orderCommon` and `lineConfig.taskPath`. I\'m handling potential conflicts by returning a 409 error with a specific error code and message. For AMR system failures, I\'m auto-unlocking the line, recording errors, and returning a 502 with relevant details. Success scenarios involve keeping the line locked and returning a 200 OK response with the order ID.\n\n\n**Adding New Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `POST /api/trigger` endpoint, ensuring the request body is validated against existing lines and stations, and that the `triggerStation` data is retrieved and used. The `amrClient.sendTrigger` method is the next focus; I\'m setting up error handling for potential failures. The `POST /api/line/reset` and `GET /api/logs` endpoints are up next. I am also working on `POST /api/test/simulate`, and integrating Vite middleware for development!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 40259596
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
