    thinking: "**Designing the Frontend**\n\nOkay, the backend is humming, and now I\'m shifting gears to the frontend. My focus is entirely on a mobile-first approach, prioritizing PDA usability. This means I\'m concentrating on designing substantial, tactile buttons, aiming for at least 60-70px in height. Clear spacing is crucial to avoid mis-taps. I\'m also putting readability under factory lighting and on small PDA screens as a top priority.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'ve been working on color schemes, aiming for high contrast and clarity. I\'m leaning toward amber/yellow or blue for \"G\341\273\214I L\341\273\206NH,\" emerald green for \"TRIGGER,\" red for emergencies, and neutral grays. Confirmation modals for commands like \"G\341\273\214I L\341\273\206NH\" and \"Reset Line\" will feature prominent \"H\341\273\246Y\" and \"X\303\201C NH\341\272\254N\" buttons. Polling will occur every 2.5 seconds. I also have an offline banner in mind.\n\nI\'ve also designed a station selector that automatically parses URLs like `/control/line-a/pickup`. If accessed via the root, it launches a station screen and includes a multi-station simulator. The last point, of course, covers communications.\n\n\n"
