  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on the UI components, specifically `src/components/ConfirmModal.tsx`. My goal is a modal dialog optimized for tactile PDA touchscreens, so I\'m concentrating on large, easily tappable buttons. The design will feature clear labeling and confirmation prompts, with distinct \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" actions. Destructive actions will be emphasized.\n\n\n**Developing Station Control**\n\nI\'ve moved on to `src/components/StationControl.tsx` now. This is the main screen for a station PDA. I\'m focusing on the header elements, including the station name/code, line status indicator, and connection status. I am working on the configuration info cards to make them compact but easy to read. Specifically, I\'m working on the two primary actions, which will be extra-large buttons with clear text and tactile feedback. One will be disabled if the line is running.\n\n\n**Implementing Status Displays**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to handle different loading states. I\'ll need a status banner with clear visual cues: green for success, red for errors, and detailed error messages. There will also be a \"Reset Line\" button with a confirmation modal and warning. I\'ll need a bottom toolbar/drawer trigger for quick station switching and communication logs. The logs drawer will show details like order ID, duration, and payloads. Finally, the station selector will be a landing screen with cards for each station and a multi-device simulator.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 671776054
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
